<article class="env-lemma" id="0D6F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D6F">Lemma <span data-tag="0D6F">21.20.2</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. Let $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$. For $K$ in $D(\mathcal{O})$ we have $H^ p(U, K) = H^ p(\mathcal{C}/U, K|_{\mathcal{C}/U})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathcal{I}^\bullet $ be a K-injective complex of $\mathcal{O}$-modules representing $K$. Then 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  H^ q(U, K) = H^ q(\Gamma (U, \mathcal{I}^\bullet )) = H^ q(\Gamma (\mathcal{C}/U, \mathcal{I}^\bullet |_{\mathcal{C}/U}))  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by construction of cohomology. By Lemma <a href="/tag/08FI" data-tag="08FI">21.20.1</a> the complex $\mathcal{I}^\bullet |_{\mathcal{C}/U}$ is a K-injective complex representing $K|_{\mathcal{C}/U}$ and the lemma follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>